   "contentDescription": "Illustration of a hand holding playing cards featuring landmarks."
  },
  {
   "type": "copyText",
   "text": "Essentials of Mexico City",
   "size": "EXTRA_LARGE",
   "variant": "HEADLINE"
  },
  {
   "type": "copyText",
   "text": "<b>24. June 2025 | 2 min read | Lufthansa Editorial Team</b>",
   "size": "SMALL",
   "variant": "BODY"
  },
  {
   "type": "copyText",
   "text": "<b>A sinking city with a flood of taxis: five things about Mexico City that will surprise you.</b>",
   "size": "MEDIUM",
   "variant": "BODY"
  },
  {
   "type": "copyText",
   "text": "<b>Take a Deep Breath</b>",
   "size": "MEDIUM",
   "variant": "BODY"
  },
  {
   "type": "copyText",
   "text": "Mexico City has launched the Hoy No Circula program to improve air quality in the city. As a result, only cars with certain numbers on their license plates are allowed to drive on certain days. But do the city's residents adhere to this? Sure, by owning multiple license plates.",
   "size": "MEDIUM",
   "variant": "BODY"
  },
  {
   "type": "image",
   "url": "https://www.lufthansa.com/content/dam/lh/article-images/mobile-app/north-america/essentials-of-mexico-city/lh_app_mexico-city_illustration1_sylvia-neuner_1920x1080.jpg.transform/lh-dcep-transform-width-1440/img.jpg",
   "contentDescription": "Left: Illustration of a vendor with number plates. Right: Illustration of a sardine tin with small taxis. "
  },
  {
   "type": "copyText",
   "text": "<b>Taxi, Please!</b>",
   "size": "MEDIUM",
   "variant": "BODY"
  },
  {
   "type": "copyText",
   "text": "The fact that Mexico City needs such a program becomes clear when you consider the number of taxis – over 140,000!",
   "size": "MEDIUM",
   "variant": "BODY"
  },
  {
   "type": "spacer",
   "size": "MEDIUM"
  },
