  {
   "type": "spacer",
   "size": "MEDIUM"
  },
  {
   "type": "copyText",
   "text": "<b>Royal Residence</b>",
   "size": "MEDIUM",
   "variant": "BODY"
  },
  {
   "type": "copyText",
   "text": "There is only one monarchical castle in North America, and it is located in Mexico City. The&nbsp;67-meter high Chapultepec Castle was built by the Spanish in 1785 and is the only residence ever used by a royal family in North America.",
   "size": "MEDIUM",
   "variant": "BODY"
  },
  {
   "type": "image",
   "url": "https://www.lufthansa.com/content/dam/lh/article-images/mobile-app/north-america/essentials-of-mexico-city/lh_app_mexico-city_illustration2_sylvia-neuner_1920x1080.jpg.transform/lh-dcep-transform-width-1440/img.jpg",
   "contentDescription": "Left: Illustration of a sandcastle builder on the beach. Right: Illustration of a hand holding playing cards featuring landmarks."
  },
  {
   "type": "copyText",
   "text": "<b>Proud Heritage</b>",
   "size": "MEDIUM",
   "variant": "BODY"
  },
  {
   "type": "copyText",
   "text": "Mexico City is proudly home to four World Heritage Sites: the historic center, Xochimilco, the former home and studio of architect Luis Barragán, and UNAM, one of the oldest and largest universities on the continent.&nbsp;",
   "size": "MEDIUM",
   "variant": "BODY"
  },
  {
   "type": "image",
   "url": "https://www.lufthansa.com/content/dam/lh/article-images/mobile-app/north-america/essentials-of-mexico-city/lh_app_mexico-city_illustration3_sylvia-neuner_1920x1080.jpg.transform/lh-dcep-transform-width-1440/img.jpg",
   "contentDescription": " Illustration of a person looking over a cliff as a straw hat falls down."
  },
  {
   "type": "copyText",
   "text": "<b>Getting to the Bottom of it</b>",
   "size": "MEDIUM",
   "variant": "BODY"
  },
  {
   "type": "copyText",
   "text": "30 to 40 cm! That's how much Mexico City sinks every year. This is due to the muddy ground on which the city sits, as it was built on a dried-up lake. And underneath that is groundwater, which is pumped out and erodes the soil. Mexico City will therefore continue to sink.",
   "size": "MEDIUM",
   "variant": "BODY"
  },
  {
   "type": "copyText",
   "text": "All illustrations © Sylvia Neuner",
   "size": "MEDIUM",
   "variant": "BODY"
  },
